\code{na_safe_group_id()}), so only NA-key rows get a unique
\code{.episode_id} and every other row keeps the normal
\code{"{facility}_{visit}"} format. \code{fallback_visit_col} is the one deliberate
exception: a row missing \code{visit_col} can still be confirmed to match
another row via a secondary identifier. The three candidate id strings are
built as plain vectors, not inside a dplyr verb, so the fallback lookup is
never attempted when no \code{fallback_visit_col} was supplied.

